{
  "id": "Compound::DB00523 - Disease::DOID:1192",
  "verbalization": "Alitretinoin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Peripheral Nervous System Neoplasm through a chain of biological relationships involving retinoic acid. The evidence suggests that Alitretinoin causes conditions such as Nail Dystrophy, Ochronosis, and Acne Fulminans, all of which are linked to Tretinoin. Tretinoin, in turn, is known to treat Peripheral Nervous System Neoplasm, indicating a potential therapeutic or pathophysiological link between these entities. The shared ancestry of Alitretinoin and Tretinoin through Retinoic Acid underscores a common biochemical pathway, suggesting that Alitretinoin may exert its effects via a similar mechanism to Tretinoin. This integrated evidence implies that Alitretinoin could potentially influence the development or progression of Peripheral Nervous System Neoplasm through retinoic acid-dependent pathways, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
